<title>AUSTRIA: OPEC MEMBERS STRONGLY COMMITED TO DEAL-COMMUNIQUE.</title>
<headline>OPEC MEMBERS STRONGLY COMMITED TO DEAL-COMMUNIQUE.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC ministers are commited to the producer's groups decision to freeze its ceiling and all individual output allocations to the end of the year, the communique states.</p>
<p>&quot;Member coutries strongly reiterated their commitment to this arrangement and made an undertaking to restrain output to their agreed level of allocation,&quot; it said.  </p>
<p>The communique also confirmed the election of Qatar's Abdullah bin Hamad al-Attiyah as President of the producer group, with Indonesia's Ida Bagus Sudjana the alternate.</p>
<p>OPEC next meets in Jakarta, Indonesia on November 26.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
